<title>USA: U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Farmer sales remain slow.</title>
<headline>U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Farmer sales remain slow.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dark northern spring wheat cash bids were higher on Thursday, underpinned by the continued slow pace of farmer selling, cash grain dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;I think it (the market) needs to rally a bit before we get much farmer selling. We need to get to about $4.00 (on March MGE spring wheat futures),&quot; one dealer said.</p>
<p>March spring wheat closed 4-1/2 cents higher at $3.82 a bushel on the Minneapolis Grain Exchange.</p>
<p>Dealers said heavy rains in the Pacific Northwest were causing some minor transport difficulties but ship and barge movements in Portland were proceeding without problems.  </p>
